ration_phone_started` | phone `TextField.onChanged` | On the first edit only, guarded by `_phoneStartedFired`. The phone number is never sent. |","+| `loan_amount_changed` `{amount: int}` | `Slider.onChangeEnd` | Once per drag or tap, when the user lets go. Skipped if the value is the same as at `onChangeStart`, e.g. after tapping the thumb without moving it. `onChanged` now only updates the UI. |","+| `terms_accepted` | `CheckboxListTile.onChanged` | When the box changes to ticked. Unticking sends nothing. |","+| `registration_continue_tapped` `{amount: int, terms: bool}` | Continue button `onPressed` | On each tap, before navigating to `/offers`. |","+| `offers_scrolled` `{offset: double}` | `offer_screen.dart`, `NotificationListener<ScrollEndNotification>` around the list | Once per scroll gesture, when scrolling stops. `offset` is `metrics.pixels`. Only the list's own scrolls count (`depth == 0`). |","+","+Verification: `flutter analyze` reports no issues. I did not run the app on a","+device or emulator, and I did not check the events in PostHog.","+","+## Which parts of the colleague's note applied","+","+This app has the same setup as the note: Flutter, `posthog_flutter` 5.x, and","+the PostHog free tier, which bills per event (see README). Its spec also uses","+the same wording (\"started typing\", \"moved the slider\", \"scrolled\"). The","+screens had no events yet, so there was nothing to fix. I used the note's","+approach when writing the code, so the problem never appears:","+","+- **Applied: once-per-visit flags for text fields.** Both `*_started` events","+  use a `bool` flag, so each one fires once, not on every keystroke.","+- **Applied: `onChangeEnd` for the slider.** Without it, one drag across the","+  49 divisions could send dozens of `loan_amount_changed` events.","+- **Applied: `ScrollEndNotification` instead of scroll updates** for","+  `offers_scrolled`.","+- **Applied: keep names and properties unchanged.** The dashboards depend on them.","+- **Not needed: firing on focus loss and `FocusNode` tap events.** No event in","+  the spec needs a field's final value, and no event is about tapping a field.","+  Also, email and phone are PII and must not be sent at all.","+- **Not used: the note's verification steps** (`PostHogConfig.debug`, PostHog →","+  Activity). They need a running app and the PostHog dashboard, and I used","+  neither.","+","+## Things to know / open choices","+","+- **\"Once\" means once per lifetime of the registration screen's state.** That","+  state stays alive while `/offers` is open on top of it. So if a user goes","+  back and edits the email again, `registration_email_started` is not sent a","+  second time. For a funnel that is probably what you want. If you want one","+  event per visit instead, reset the flags when the user returns to the screen.","+- **`offers_scrolled` fires once per scroll gesture, not once per visit.**","+  This keeps the offset data useful. If you only need it as a funnel step,","+  adding a once-per-visit flag would cut the volume further.","+- **`terms_accepted` fires again if the user unticks and ticks again.** This is","+  rare and cheap. Add a flag if you want it to fire only once."]}],"created":true},{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-cQ8atX/analysis_options.yaml","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":10,"newStart":1,"newLines":1,"lines":["-analyzer:","-  exclude:","-    - build/**","-    - android/**","-    - ios/**","-    - web/**","-    - windows/**","-    - macos/**","-    - linux/**"," include: package:flutter_lints/flutter.yaml"]}]}],"moreFiles":1,"changedFiles":["/private/tmp/h-cQ8atX/.dart_tool/package_config.json","/private/tmp/h-cQ8atX/.dart_tool/package_graph.json","/private/tmp/h-cQ8atX/.dart_tool/version","/private/tmp/h-cQ8atX/ANSWER.md","/private/tmp/h-cQ8atX/analysis_options.yaml","/private/tmp/h-cQ8atX/pubspec.lock"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0153QD7t6hBdeyE76gHVBnaX","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reas