{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgSDUFEqa6G2HYjo9XkeN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added all six events from `docs/EVENTS.md` to the registration and offers screens. They all go through `Analytics.capture`, with names and properties exactly as in the spec. `flutter analyze` finds no issues, but I haven't run the app or checked the events in PostHog.\n\nThe colleague's note applied, because this app is on PostHog's free tier, which bills per event, and the spec uses the same wording. The screens had no events yet, so nothing needed fixing; I just wired them so they don't fire on every change:\n- **Email and phone started:** each fires once, on the first edit, not on every keystroke. Neither event sends the email or phone number.\n- **Loan amount changed:** fires when the user lets go of the slider, so once per drag instead of once per step. It's skipped if the value didn't actually change.\n- **Terms accepted:** fires when the box is ticked, not when it's unticked.\n- **Continue tapped:** fires on each tap, with `amount` and `terms`.\n- **Offers scrolled:** fires once each time scrolling stops, with the offset.\n\nParts of the note didn't apply. No event needs a field's final value or a tap on a field, so there was no need for focus-based events. And its checks in the PostHog dashboard need a running app.\n\nThree choices you might want to change (also listed in ANSWER.md):\n- **Email and phone \"once\":** this lasts as long as the registration screen stays alive, which includes time spent on the offers screen. A user who goes back and edits the email won't send the event again.\n- **Offers scrolled:** fires on every scroll, not once per visit. If you only need it as a funnel step, a once-per-visit flag would cut the number of events.\n- **Terms accepted:** fires again if someone unticks and ticks the box again.\n\nRunning `flutter analyze` rewrote `analysis_options.yaml` and created some build files. I reverted and deleted those, so the only changes are the two screen files and the new `ANSWER.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1728,"cache_read_input_tokens":30502,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1728},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d74a1e58-437a-471c-be99-c83e6653ecb3","uuid":"c8cfc401-1d0a-4fd6-8c90-ed4ebf824c84","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:48:22.380Z","request_id":"req_011CgSDUEyUcFAmwttEvgfjT"}
